  "live_records": {
    "q-148384": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148384",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The variances of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ are $5$ and $20$, respectively. Given that $\\text{Cov}(X,Y)=8,$ find the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{5}, \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[Y]}=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[X]} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
