    "q-148381": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148381",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=120,$ $\\text{SD}[X]=10,$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]=15$, find the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & =\\frac{120}{10\\cdot 15} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
