    "q-146468": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146468",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=5,$ $\\text{SD}[X]=2,$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]=4$, find the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nSubstituting our data in the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
