    "q-148350": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148350",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{11}{18},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2582,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2664,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot (4{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}xy)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{4}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{12}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-(\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{11}{18}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(\\frac{1}{108})}{(0.2582)\\cdot (0.2664)} \\\\  & ≈0.13,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
