    "q-148337": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148337",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{9},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{5}{9},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.5329,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2833,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot \\frac{x+y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-(\\frac{11}{9})(\\frac{5}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{81})}{(0.5329)\\cdot (0.2833)} \\\\  & ≈-0.08,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
